  "publishedAt": "2026-10-23T00:00:00Z",
  "snippet": "#​494 — October 23, 2026 Read on the Web React Status TanStack Start Reaches 1.0 After a year as a release candidate, TanStack Start 1.0 is officially stable. Tanner Linsley explains how it grew out of TanStack Router, a...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ejihjkazanj4b02abevr.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​494 — October 23, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191925/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #333;\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 2.7em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.3em; margin-bottom: 0px;\"> React Status</div>\n</div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191882/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ejihjkazanj4b02abevr.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>TanStack Start Reaches 1.0</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>After a year as a release candidate, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191882/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">TanStack Start 1.0 is officially stable</a>. Tanner Linsley explains how it grew out of <em>TanStack Router</em>, and is candid about RSC, which felt like <em>\"this box we had to check to be taken seriously as a React framework\"</em>, and which <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191926/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">tanstack.com</a> itself no longer uses. Plus:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>📊 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191883/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">The same app in Start and Next.js 16.4, benchmarked</a> – <em>Start</em> handled 2.9x-8.6x more dynamic requests and built ~1.7x faster with type-checking included.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🚚 Moving over? There are official guides for <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191884/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">migrating from Next.js</a> and <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191885/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">from the RC</a>. Sarthak Mishra <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191886/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">moved his site over from Astro</a> (and explains why) and Lovable offers older projects a migration option (<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191887/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">here's how one went</a>).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>💬 Ryan Carniato called it <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191888/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>\"a React metaframework with an architecture I can get behind\"</em></a>, while in <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191889/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">the r/reactjs thread</a> Tanner explained why '1.0' is listed as <code>1.169</code> on npm.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191927/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"120\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/927c2926.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"120\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191927/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"master.dev\">TypeScript in the Age of AI</a></span> — Knowing TypeScript deeply is how you get better code out of AI. Adam Rackis of Spotify shows you how to steer AI toward simpler, correct types and catch the mistakes it slips in.</p>\n<p>Master.dev <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ Last week, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191890/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Next.js patched two critical RCEs</a>, one rooted in React Server Components, and <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191891/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">a public PoC</a> is now out. Update Next.js to 16.4.1 or 15.5.28; for other RSC setups, update the <code>react-server-dom-*</code> packages to 19.3.1 (or 19.2.9/19.1.10/19.0.9).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191892/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React DevTools for agents now has official docs</a>, covering how it exposes profiling and component data to coding agents through Chrome DevTools MCP.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191893/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo SDK 58</a> is out, using the new <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191894/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native 0.88</a>, targeting iOS 27 and ready for the iPhone Duo on day one.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191895/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native for Web has active maintainers again</a> and is moving to the React Foundation's GitHub org.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191896/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">TypeScript 7.1 is now in beta</a>, adding a programmatic API and more speed. Type-checking MUI's docs is 1.9x faster and uses half the memory.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191897/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nextjs.org\">Improving Navigation Experience in v0 with Next.js 16.4</a></span> — How the Next.js team used Partial Prefetching, intent-based prefetching and the new <code>navigation()</code> API to cut loading skeletons across its <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191898/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">v0</a> AI app builder.</p>\n<p>Aurora Scharff (Vercel) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191899/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"building.owner.com\">React Only Where Needed: Owner's Next.js to Astro Move</a></span> — Owner's 10,000+ restaurant sites now run on Astro and Cloudflare Workers, keeping React for interactive islands. Menu-page p75 LCP went from 5.4s to 0.7s.</p>\n<p>Selden and Hanford (Owner) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191900/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tkdodo.eu\">Dead Code Shouldn't Exist</a></span> — The slides and transcript from a popular talk Dominik has given at several conferences this year on how Sentry removed 28K lines of unused code with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191901/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Knip</a>.</p>\n<p>Dominik Dorfmeister </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🤖 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191902/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Testing AI-Generated Code: Lint the Pattern, Test the Decision</a> – Structural lint rules and shared harnesses beat a test beside every component. <cite>Robin Wieruch</cite></p>\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191903/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Apple Didn't Invent the Foldable. It Might Make You Support One.</a> – Getting a React Native app ready for the iPhone Duo's three compatibility tiers. <cite>Sean Barker (Infinite Red)</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191904/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Loading a 9MB WebAssembly Module Earlier Made Recraft's Editor 17% Faster</a> – Suspending components left the module's download waiting its turn in the React tree. <cite>Sergey Patrakeev (Recraft)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠  Code, Tools &amp; Libraries</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191905/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/nishfkuexsqapfi2rcgp.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191905/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"pixelgui.com\">Pixel: Build Graphical Applications in the Terminal</a></span> — Like <em>Ink</em>, but with \"pixel perfect\" graphics. It's a React renderer that draws rounded corners, gradients and proper fonts in terminals that support the Kitty graphics protocol, and that can even embed Chromium WebViews to run web apps in a pane(!)</p>\n<p>Rob Pruzan (Zenbu Labs) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191906/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tanstack.com\">TanStack Hotkeys Beta: A Type-Safe Library for Keyboard Shortcuts</a></span> — <em>Hotkeys</em> takes care of the fiddly, cross-platform edge cases of keyboard shortcuts, sequences, and user-recorded hotkeys. The beta adds <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191907/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">scopes</a>, so that, say, a dialog's <code>Escape</code> doesn't close the panel behind it. Try the demo on the homepage.</p>\n<p>TanStack </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191908/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"reactrouter.com\">React Router 8.5 Hands View Transitions Over to React</a></span> — Its own view transition APIs are deprecated in favor of React 19.3's <code>&lt;ViewTransition&gt;</code>. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191909/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Migrating</a> starts with wrapping an <code>&lt;Outlet&gt;</code> and removing the old props and state styling. There's also an unstable <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191910/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">'API-only' mode</a> that serves static HTML but keeps a server for loaders and actions.</p>\n<p>Remix Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191911/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1792586346/br715i8krli31hn0g9bi.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191911/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.env.style\">env.style: Style Every Environment with Colors or Custom Icons</a></span> — A utility that wraps your Next.js config or Vite setup to tint the favicon per environment at build time, so you can see at a glance where you are.</p>\n<p>Ryan George </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191912/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"tamagui.dev\">Tamagui 3: One React UI Codebase for Web and Native</a></span> — A styling system and UI kit for sharing one codebase between React web apps and React Native. v3 adds an opt-in (beta) C++ native runtime that applies theme changes without re-rendering, plus React Strict DOM and Tailwind-style syntax.</p>\n<p>Nate Wienert </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191913/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Hydrogen 2026.10</a> – Shopify's commerce toolkit is now a library you can drop into existing Next.js or React Router apps.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191914/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Morphicons 2.0</a> – Spring-physics morphing between SVG icons. Now filled icons morph too, not just stroked ones. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191915/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">See it in action on its homepage</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191916/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Unistyles 3.6</a> – High-performance React Native styling library. Now with an experimental zero-config Metro integration instead of the Babel plugin.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191917/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Motion 14.6</a> – Adds keyboard grab-and-move to <code>Reorder</code> lists, plus <code>stepFrames</code> for deterministic animation testing.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>Build and deploy durable AI agents in TypeScript, without managing your own infrastructure. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191918/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Ship your first agent with Trigger.dev</a>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191919/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo is mobile AI infrastructure</a>: Your agents build, test and ship iOS and Android apps, and you approve what goes out. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191919/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Try it</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🎶  And finally… make a little noise</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191920/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/dtm0yamwanrjkzjtlgke.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>Fancy making a little music with React? <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191920/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Strudel Flow 2</a> is an open source React app built with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191921/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Flow</a> and <code>shadcn/ui</code>. Connect instruments and effects to generate <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191922/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Strudel</a> code, or load a community patch and start turning knobs.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191923/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">source code</a> offers a neat extension point: define an instrument or effect in a small <code>.node.ts</code> file, then supply a React component for a custom interface. As <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/191924/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">the team says</a>, <em>\"coding is a fun thing to do for its own sake.\"</em> 🤘</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}